/p><div><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi Joe,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Are you using multinomPois() or gmultmix()? Can you show some of the code you used to format the data and fit the model?<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Richard<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">On Fri, Jan 4, 2013 at 1:46 PM, &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jcl...@utk.edu</a>&gt; wrote:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi Andy, <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">No, but I do have some negative numbers for obsCovs (minutes from sunrise).\r\n<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Regardless, I get the same message when I run the model without any covariates...<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br>\r\nOn Friday, January 4, 2013 12:10:54 PM UTC-5, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">\r\njcl...@utk.edu</a> wrote:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border:none;border-left:solid #cccccc 1.0pt;padding:0in 0in 0in 6.0pt;margin-left:4.8pt;margin-right:0in\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I&#39;m trying to fit a removal model and I keep getting the following error message:<br>\r\nError in dpois(x, lambda, log) : <br>\r\n  Non-numeric argument to mathematical function<br>\r\nAnyone know what this is about?<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thanks!<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Joe<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\